            ^"Abilities" STRING "Arabic 5 (mercantile matters), Mediterranean Lore 4 (personalities), Artes Liberales 3 (arithmetic), Bargain 4 (silk), Carouse 3 (power drinking), Charm 4 (being witty), Common Law 2 (exchequer law), Etiquette 3 (merchant society), Folk Ken 4 (merchants), French 4 (mercantile matters), Guile 4 (lying about weights and measures), Hebrew 5 (prayers and blessings), Intrigue 3 (the muqta’s enemies), Italian 4 (mercantile matters), Judaic Lore 2 (poetry), Latin 2 (academic usage), Leadership 3 (intimidation), Merchant 5 +2 (silk), Persian 5 (mercantile matters), Philosophiae 1 (moral philosophy), Slavic 1 (mercantile matters), Spanish 4 (mercantile matters), Theology: Judaism 2 (mitzvot)"
            ^"Equipment" STRING "Letters of credit, pouches of money, bodyguards, outer clothes with a Jewish badge emblazoned upon them"
            ^"Notes" STRING "The Radhanite merchant is a wealthy man in his own right, but serves one richer and more powerful still."
            ^"Source" STRING "Realms of Power: The Divine"
